# Directory listing exposure: Express serveIndex() publishes a browsable file
# listing of a server directory over HTTP. Unless the directory is deliberately
# public, this leaks file names, structure, and often sensitive artifacts
# (logs, keys, backups) — information disclosure (CWE-548).
#
# Found via OWASP Juice Shop's own author markers (2026-09-26):
#   server.ts:288  app.use('/ftp', ..., serveIndex('ftp', { icons: true })) // vuln-line directoryListingChallenge
#   server.ts:300  app.use('/support/logs', ..., serveIndex('logs', ...))   // vuln-line accessLogDisclosureChallenge
# keur had no directory-listing rule.
#
# Match a serveIndex(...) call (the middleware that renders the listing).
id: KEUR-INFO-001
maturity: 2
title: Directory listing exposed over HTTP via serveIndex()
category: data-exposure
severity: warning
engine: pattern
action: warn
target:
  extensions: .js .ts .mjs
patterns:
  - regex: \bserveIndex\s*\(
    message: serveIndex() publishes a browsable directory listing over HTTP (CWE-548). This leaks file names/structure and often sensitive files (logs, keys, backups). Serve only intentionally-public dirs, and never expose logs/keys/config directories.
confidence: 0.65
fix: Remove serveIndex for any directory that is not deliberately public. Serve specific files explicitly instead of a browsable index, and keep logs/keys/backups out of any web-served path.
